{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress inward, reducing electrode swelling. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, while minimizing thickness expansion to 13.1% after 50 cycles.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The design reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles, enabling scalable production for battery applications"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore engineering as a scalable strategy for developing mechanically stable silicon-carbon anodes with minimal expansion, advancing practical lithium-ion battery electrode design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. The resulting atlas identified 100+ brain cell subclasses and defined active, primed, and repressive chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 define distinct repression mechanisms. The resource enables deep learning models for predicting cell-type-specific epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas spans over 100 brain cell subclasses using integrated single-cell epigenomic profiling",
    "Active chromatin states marked by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal epigenomic atlas provides a comprehensive framework for annotating the brain regulatory genome and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through cell-type-specific epigenomic features."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates factors influencing early human settlement in desert regions, focusing on the role of stone availability alongside water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across the Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials where freshwater existed but stone was scarce. The results indicate that early human settlement patterns were constrained by the co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, not water alone, with implications for understanding Pleistocene dispersal models across multiple continents.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Palaeolake deposits were present at 55 of 125 surveyed localities but no lithic artefacts or knappable stone were found in areas with abundant freshwater",
    "Spatial modeling shows 57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, and raw-material availability improves site discrimination accuracy to 0.768",
    "Convergent patterns across Africa, North America, and Asia suggest stone availability constraints are a universal factor in Pleistocene human dispersal"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that lithic resource availability, not water alone, was a critical constraint on early human settlement in arid regions, refining models of Pleistocene dispersal across continents."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and IL-23-driven gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion reduced ILC3 numbers and increased enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive intestinal inflammation through PRKAR1A modulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how adsorbate bonding at platinum surfaces extends beyond the adsorption site due to delocalized electronic bands. Using velocity-resolved kinetics, researchers measured bond strength changes of three molecules across 100 angstroms of step-step distance on Pt, finding variations up to 0.2 eV. The results highlight molecule-specific orbital hybridization with metal bands, influencing bond strength through structural modifications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Bond strength variations of up to 0.2 eV observed across 100 angstroms of step-step distance on platinum",
    "Molecule-specific orbital hybridization with symmetry-selected metal bands",
    "Structural modifications of the metal surface directly impact molecule-metal bond strength"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that electronic delocalization in catalytic metal surfaces significantly influences adsorbate bond strength over large structural scales, providing insights into surface reactivity mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record power-conversion efficiencies of 24.84% in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules while maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, increasing moisture vulnerability",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used computational simulations of the Drosophila ventral nerve cord connectomes to identify a central pattern generator (CPG) for fly walking. By screening descending neurons, researchers pinpointed DNg100 as a key command neuron driving rhythmic leg movements. Simulations revealed a minimal three-neuron circuit—comprising one inhibitory and two excitatory interneurons—that generates coordinated leg rhythms across all six legs and is necessary and sufficient for rhythmic motor output. The findings provide cellular and synaptic details of a CPG circuit for walking in flies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "DNg100 acts as a command neuron driving rhythmic leg motor activity in flies",
    "A minimal three-neuron circuit (one inhibitory, two excitatory interneurons) generates coordinated leg rhythms across all six legs",
    "A separate descending pathway (DNb08) was identified as a driver of rhythmic leg movements, confirmed via optogenetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies the first cellular-level CPG circuit for walking in any animal, advancing understanding of how rhythmic motor patterns emerge from neural circuits."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the similarities and differences between bird and human vocalizations, focusing on shared acoustic features and the evidence supporting analogies. The authors analyzed vocal characteristics to determine how comparable these systems are, finding that while some features are similar, the evidence for certain analogies is insufficient. The results highlight the need for more robust evidence when drawing parallels between bird and human communication.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Some acoustic features of bird and human vocalizations are comparable",
    "Certain analogies between bird and human vocalizations lack sufficient evidence",
    "The study identifies gaps in the evidence supporting vocalization comparisons"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings underscore the importance of rigorous evidence when drawing parallels between avian and human vocal communication systems, contributing to a more nuanced understanding of cross-species vocalization similarities."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with long-range ordered nanostructures. The approach uses high shear forces to align nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices, enabling scalable production of complex 3D architectures. Results show 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid filaments achieve zero volume shrinkage post-sintering, with tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) and mechanical properties.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing enables high-loading nanocomposites (up to 55 wt% boron nitride) with long-range ordered nanostructures",
    "Post-sintering materials exhibit zero volume shrinkage and exceptional thermomechanical stability",
    "Vertically aligned composites show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K), while horizontally aligned structures provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This method bridges nanoscale nanofiller alignment with macroscale geometries, enabling scalable fabrication of high-performance nanocomposites for thermal management and structural applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how tandem repeat (TR) variations influence immune cell-specific gene expression using whole-genome and single-cell RNA sequencing across 1,925 individuals. It identifies over 69,000 single-cell expression quantitative trait loci, 30.7% specific to immune cell types, and links TRs to chromatin accessibility and genetic associations with immune traits through multiomic analyses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of 69,000 single-cell expression quantitative trait loci (eQTLs) with 30.7% immune cell type specificity",
    "TRs implicated in 1,490 candidate causal drivers of gene expression across 6.1% of tested genes",
    "TR-mediated regulation connects to 200+ genes associated with immune and haematological traits"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes tandem repeats as major regulators of cell type-specific gene expression and complex trait architecture in the human immune system through large-scale multiomic profiling."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether a small molecule could enhance cellular fitness in mitochondria-diseased cells. The approach involved identifying a compound that mitigates mitochondrial stress responses. Results showed the molecule improved cell viability and metabolic function in diseased mitochondria, suggesting potential therapeutic applications for mitochondrial disorders.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A small molecule improved cellular fitness in mitochondria-diseased cells",
    "The molecule mitigated mitochondrial stress responses",
    "Enhanced metabolic function and cell viability in diseased mitochondria"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate a small molecule's capacity to counteract mitochondrial dysfunction, offering a potential mechanism for targeting mitochondrial diseases."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. A highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst was developed using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx system achieved stoichiometric pure water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitride/oxynitride photocatalysts. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and surface kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric pure water splitting at 420 nm",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and surface reaction kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over nitride/oxynitride materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing solar-driven water splitting technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the genetic architecture of Alzheimer's disease using multi-ancestry genomic data. By analyzing 109,479 cases and 2.1 million controls, the researchers identified 118 risk loci, including 48 novel ones. They found that AD-associated genetic risk factors disproportionately affect microglial and neuronal pathways, with improved polygenic prediction and a SNP heritability estimate of :16%.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of 118 Alzheimer's disease risk loci across diverse ancestries, including 48 novel loci",
    "Genetic risk factors significantly enrich microglial upregulation and neuronal downregulation pathways",
    "SNP heritability estimate of 16%, nearly threefold higher than prior estimates"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that common genetic variants contribute substantially more to Alzheimer's disease risk than previously estimated, revealing critical cellular mechanisms and potential therapeutic targets."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how the chirality of magnetic excitations defines altermagnets, a class of materials with non-collinear magnetic order. Using theoretical modeling, the research demonstrates that the handedness of collective magnetic excitations serves as a fundamental identifier for altermagnets, providing a clear criterion for their classification based on magnetic properties.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Altermagnets are characterized by the handedness of their collective magnetic excitations",
    "Theoretical modeling establishes chirality as a defining property for altermagnets",
    "This approach offers a clear classification criterion for altermagnets based on magnetic excitations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides a fundamental criterion for identifying altermagnets through the chirality of their magnetic excitations, advancing understanding of non-collinear magnetic order in materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how 3D ordered macroporous Cu-based multimetallic alloys improve electrocatalytic CO2 reduction to eth. The catalyst, constructed via CuOx with multimetallic alloy surfaces, achieves 64.1% Faradic efficiency for ethylene at -1.55 V vs RHE. In-situ analyses show enhanced surface electric fields, local pH, and mass transport, enabling asymmetric *CO-*CHO coupling through electronic heterogeneity at Cuδ+ sites.",
  "key_findings": [
    "64.1% Faradic efficiency for ethylene at -1.55 V vs RHE",
    "Enhanced surface electric fields and local pH from 3DOM structure",
    "Asymmetric *CO-*CHO coupling via electronic heterogeneity at Cuδ+ sites"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes atomic-level design principles for Cu-based multimetallic alloys to control *CO adsorption and hydrogenation pathways, enhancing ethylene selectivity in CO2 electroreduction."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window prevents amplification. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils expressing Nlrp3 and Il1b, which license pathogenic TH17 cells. After recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. The findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory through neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β axis activation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates acute type 17 skin inflammation to chronic obesity levels",
    "HFD outside the 4-day window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during this window prevents inflammatory amplification",
    "Neutrophil recruitment expressing Nlrp3 and Il1b licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, leading to persistent tissue-resident memory T cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that short-lived dietary states during specific temporal windows can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β axis critical for inflammatory disease trajectory."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated cerebellar development disparities between preterm and term children, using longitudinal neuroimaging and cognitive assessments. Findings revealed persistent structural differences in cerebellar morphology into early childhood, suggesting that prematurity impacts cerebellar maturation trajectories beyond infancy. The results highlight the need for continued monitoring of cerebellar development in preterm children.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Persistent cerebellar structural differences between preterm and term children into early childhood",
    "Prematurity influences cerebellar matinuration trajectories beyond infancy",
    "Longitudinal neuroimaging and cognitive assessments identified cerebellar morphology discrepancies"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that cerebellar development trajectories diverge between preterm and term children, providing evidence for prolonged neurodevelopmental consequences of prematurity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a minimalistic aqueous synthesis of a Cu2+-based ionic metal-organic network using 2,4,6-trinitrobenzene-1,3,5-triol (TNPG). The resulting 2D woven architecture features distorted octahedral and square planar coordination geometries, stabilized by hydrogen bonding. The framework demonstrates efficient visible-light-driven CO2 reduction with 85% selectivity for CO over H2, attributed to high charge separation and structural modulations.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A 2D woven architecture stabilized by hydrogen bonding",
    "High charge separation efficiency enabling visible-light-driven CO2 reduction",
    "85% selectivity for CO over H2 with structural modulations enhancing performance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a minimalistic strategy for designing ionic metal-organic networks with tunable electronic properties for efficient CO2 reduction, advancing supramolecular frameworks for sustainable catalysis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates irreversible metal-to-ligand charge transfer (MLCT) fragmentation in copper-heteroaryl sulfone complexes under visible light. The research demonstrates that MLCT excitation triggers C-S bond cleavage, generating carbon-centered radicals without substrate dependence. Key findings include the production of fluoroalkyl and non-fluorinated alkyl radicals, enabling copper-catalyzed C-H fluoroalkylation and radical perfluorocyclobutylation-iodination reactions. The work provides a method for synthesizing perfluorocyclobutyl motifs via halogen-atom transfer.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Copper-heteroaryl sulfone complexes undergo irreversible MLCT-driven C-S bond cleavage under visible light",
    "Generation of fluoroalkyl and non-fluorinated tertiary, secondary, and primary alkyl radicals",
    "Application in copper-catalyzed C-H fluoroalkylation and radical perfluorocyclobutylation-iodination of alkenes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a method for generating diverse carbon radicals via irreversible MLCT fragmentation, enabling new strategies for incorporating perfluorocyclobutyl groups into organic molecules through radical-based transformations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines how wearable neurotechnologies are being used by companies to train AI brain models without user consent. The research highlights the lack of transparency in data collection practices, raising ethical concerns about brain data privacy. The findings indicate significant risks to individual privacy in the emerging neurotechnology landscape.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Companies deploy wearable neurotechnologies to train AI brain models without user notification",
    "Data collection practices lack transparency, posing privacy risks",
    "The study identifies ethical concerns in the absence of user consent for brain data"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work underscores critical ethical challenges in neurotechnology data collection, emphasizing the need for transparent user consent mechanisms in AI brain model development."
}

{
  "summary": "This review compares natural and artificial photosynthesis systems, focusing on light harvesting, charge separation, catalytic conversion, and system integration. It highlights that natural photosynthesis operates at sub-percent solar-to-biomass efficiencies, while selected artificial systems achieve double-digit solar-to-fuel efficiencies under specific conditions. The study emphasizes functional differences and provides design principles for efficient solar-to-chemical conversion.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Natural photosynthesis achieves sub-percent solar-to-biomass efficiency",
    "Artificial photosynthetic devices reach double-digit solar-to-fuel efficiencies under defined conditions",
    "Artificial systems excel in spectral, interfacial, and catalytic control, while natural systems maintain regulation and repair mechanisms"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes functional distinctions between natural and artificial photosynthesis systems, providing foundational insights for designing efficient, scalable solar-to-chemical conversion technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how intervertebral discs (IVDs) integrate nanoscale fibril mechanics with fibre-scale organization under load. Using TomoSAXS, a novel 3D X-ray scattering technique, researchers mapped fibril-to-fibre mechanics in intact tissue. Key results include inverse relationships between intrafibrillar pre-strain and fibril strain, lamellar texture of pre-strain, and critical roles of annulus fibrosus-nucleus pulposus interfaces in local mechanics. These findings elucidate load-sharing mechanisms maintaining IVD elasticity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Intrafibrillar molecular pre-strain (D-period stagger) exhibits lamellar texture and correlates tightly with microscale fibre strain",
    "Pre-strain inversely relates to fibril strain and its variability, indicating load-sharing through molecular unwinding",
    "Radial strain bridges and high-curvature zones at annulus fib: fibrosus-nucleus pulposus interfaces regulate local mechanics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "TomoSAXS provides a platform for visualizing nanoscale-to-microscale matrix mechanics in fibrous materials, advancing understanding of biomechanical equilibrium in biological and engineered systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the ethical implications of fatigue-monitoring technologies deployed by construction and mining companies to enhance worker safety. The research examines how such devices impact worker privacy, highlighting concerns raised by critics regarding potential privacy threats. The findings indicate that while these technologies aim to improve safety, they may inadvertently compromise workers' privacy rights without sufficient safeguards.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fatigue-monitoring devices used in construction and mining sectors aim to improve worker safety",
    "Critics argue these technologies pose significant privacy risks to workers",
    "The study identifies a tension between safety benefits and privacy concerns in industrial settings"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The research underscores the critical balance between technological safety interventions and privacy protection in high-risk occupational environments, contributing to broader discussions on ethical technology deployment."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a glycan-targeted nanoparticle system (ICT@APD) to reprogram microglia post-spinal cord injury (SCI). The approach uses 2,5-anhydro-D-mannitol to enhance icaritin delivery, promoting anti-inflammatory microglial phenotypes. Results show improved axon regeneration, neuronal survival, and locomotor recovery in SCI models. The strategy offers a scalable platform for CNS disorders with narrow therapeutic windows.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ICT@AP:APD nanoparticles functionalized with 2,5-anhydro-D-mannitol enable selective microglial uptake",
    "Icaritin reprogramming shifts microglia to anti-inflammatory phenotypes",
    "SCI models exhibit enhanced axon regeneration and locomotor recovery with the targeted approach"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This glycan-mediated microglial targeting strategy provides a scalable platform for reprogramming dysfunctional microglia in spinal cord injury, advancing therapeutic approaches for central nervous system disorders with narrow therapeutic windows."
}
